{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 37, :comments ["<b>שמר</b> — And now set your heart and observe: <i>observe the blameless man and look at the upright man</i>; you will always see their future — peace." "And behold, <b>תם</b> — <i>שלום</i> follows it, as though it were written: 'for the future of the blameless man is peace.'"], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 37, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:30:03.767674592Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}